   "player/README.md": "# RetroFM player (boom box UI)\n\nSelf-contained front end for RetroFM. Open `index.html` to run it. No build step, no dependencies.\n\n```\nplayer/\n  index.html        markup\n  player.css        styles\n  player.js         all behavior (no inline scripts, Manifest V3 friendly)\n  images/           boom-box-white.png, boom-box-black.png (1408x768, dial/needles already cleaned)\n  logos/            1960s-white.png, 1960s-black.png ... 2020s-white.png, 2020s-black.png\n```\nUse lowercase names everywhere (paths are case sensitive in extensions and on servers).\n\n## What the user does\n1. Types a date (month name, Jan/Sept style abbreviations, misspellings like \"Marrch\", or 7/4/1978). Valid range: 1960 to today. Enter or Tab moves to the genre step.\n2. Picks a genre (up/down arrows or click the genre row). The genre list depends on the decade of the date. Enter tunes in.\n3. The green display then shows `[DATE] [GENRE]` (click either to edit), the FM frequency, and the song (title and artist fade in turn; the small dot turns that off).\n4. Play / Pause / Stop on the cassette deck, Volume and Balance dials, tuning dial (hops to other genre stations of the same decade). Clicking the logo toggles light/dark.\n\n## Events the player sends (on `document`, data in `event.detail`)\n| event | detail | meaning |\n|---|---|---|\n| `retrofm:select` | `{date:'1978-07-04', year, decade, genre, frequency}` | user pressed Enter on the genre step. Find a song released BEFORE this date |\n| `retrofm:tune` | `{decade, frequency, genre\\|null, locked}` | dial moved onto a station (or between stations, genre null) |\n| `retrofm:update` | `{}` | user went back to edit the date or genre |\n| `retrofm:transport` | `{state:'playing'\\|'paused'\\|'stopped'}` | user pressed a transport button |\n| `retrofm:volume` | `{value: 0..1}` | volume dial |\n| `retrofm:balance` | `{value: -1..1}` | balance dial (-1 = full left) |\n| `retrofm:theme` | `{dark: bool}` | logo toggled light/dark |\n| `retrofm:previous` | `{}` | user clicked REWIND (symbol flashes). Not wired to anything yet |\n| `retrofm:next` | `{}` | user clicked FAST FORWARD (symbol flashes). Not wired to anything yet |\n| `retrofm:record` | `{on: bool}` | user clicked RECORD (latches on/off). Planned: request a song by typing its name |\n| `retrofm:display` | `{open: bool}` | green display expanded/collapsed |\n\n## Calls into the player\n- `RetroFM.setSong({title, artist})` shows the song on the display. Call it once the YouTube song is chosen.\n- `RetroFM.setSongYear(year)` switches the logo to that song's decade.\n- `RetroFM.setTransport('playing'|'paused'|'stopped')` updates buttons, lit symbols, reels and meters WITHOUT sending a `retrofm:transport` event (use when YouTube state changes by itself, e.g. a song ends).\n- Alternative: dispatch `retrofm:song` with `{title, artist, year}`.\n\n## Settings at the top of `player.js` sections\n- `BUTTONS = {rewind, forward, record}` in `player.js`: set any to `false` to disable that button entirely (no click area, no event).\n- `DEMO = true` shows a placeholder song about a second after tuning in. Set `false` when real songs are wired up.\n- `LOGO_BASE = 'logos/'`, `BOX_BASE = 'images/'`.\n- `ST` holds the genres and FM frequency per decade (1960s-2020s). Edit there.\n\n## Notes for the extension\n- The VU meters are simulated (the audio plays in YouTube, so there is nothing to analyze). They react to play/pause, Volume and Balance.\n- The window is designed at 450px wide and scales to fit the width and height of whatever window it is in, with no scrolling.\n- A normal browser-action popup closes when it loses focus. For a small window that stays open while working, open it with `chrome.windows.create({url:'player/index.html', type:'popup', width:450, height:520})` or use the side panel.\n- Wiring: on `retrofm:select` pick a song, play it on YouTube, then call `RetroFM.setSong(...)`. Map `retrofm:volume` / `retrofm:balance` / `retrofm:transport` to the existing VolumeController and YouTube controls.\n",
-  "player/yt_main_world.js": "// RetroFM YouTube Main-World Player Bridge\n// Runs in world: \"MAIN\" with direct access to YouTube's player API (.html5-video-player / #movie_player)\n\n(function () {\n  if (window.__retroFmMainWorldLoaded) return;\n  window.__retroFmMainWorldLoaded = true;\n\n  const EVENT_SET_VOLUME = 'RETROFM_SET_YT_VOLUME';\n  const EVENT_VOLUME_STATUS = 'RETROFM_YT_VOLUME_STATUS';\n  const STORAGE_KEY_SAVED_VOLUME = 'retrofm_saved_master_volume';\n\n  // Restore remembered master volume from localStorage if available\n  let queuedVolume = null;\n  try {\n    const saved = localStorage.getItem(STORAGE_KEY_SAVED_VOLUME);\n    if (saved !== null) {\n      const parsed = parseInt(saved, 10);\n      if (!isNaN(parsed) && parsed >= 0 && parsed <= 100) {\n        queuedVolume = parsed;\n      }\n    }\n  } catch (e) {}\n\n  let playerFound = false;\n  let navigationMuted = false;\n  let muteSafetyTimer = null;\n\n  function getPlayer() {\n    return document.querySelector('.html5-video-player') ||\n           document.getElementById('movie_player') ||\n           null;\n  }\n\n  function clearMuteSafety() {\n    if (muteSafetyTimer) {\n      clearTimeout(muteSafetyTimer);\n      muteSafetyTimer = null;\n    }\n  }\n\n  function applyVolume(vol, reason = 'direct') {\n    if (typeof vol !== 'number' || isNaN(vol)) return;\n    const clampedVol = Math.max(0, Math.min(100, Math.round(vol)));\n    queuedVolume = clampedVol;\n\n    try {\n      localStorage.setItem(STORAGE_KEY_SAVED_VOLUME, String(clampedVol));\n    } catch (e) {}\n\n    const player = getPlayer();\n    if (player && typeof player.setVolume === 'function') {\n      try {\n        const prevVol = typeof player.getVolume === 'function' ? player.getVolume() : 'unknown';\n        player.setVolume(clampedVol);\n\n        // If temporarily muted during navigation, or player is muted while target > 0, unMute now\n        if (clampedVol > 0 && typeof player.isMuted === 'function' && player.isMuted()) {\n          if (typeof player.unMute === 'function') {\n            player.unMute();\n          }\n        }\n        navigationMuted = false;\n        clearMuteSafety();\n\n        const resultingVol = typeof player.getVolume === 'function' ? player.getVolume() : clampedVol;\n        console.log(\n          `[RetroFM MainWorld] [${new Date().toISOString()}] setVolume called: requested=${clampedVol} (reason=${reason}, prev=${prevVol}) -> player.getVolume()=${resultingVol}`\n        );\n\n        broadcastStatus();\n      } catch (err) {\n        console.warn(`[RetroFM MainWorld] Error calling setVolume on player:`, err);\n      }\n    } else {\n      console.log(\n        `[RetroFM MainWorld] [${new Date().toISOString()}] Player not yet ready. Queued volume: ${clampedVol} (reason=${reason})`\n      );\n    }\n  }\n\n  function broadcastStatus() {\n    const player = getPlayer();\n    let currentVol = 100;\n    let isMuted = false;\n\n    if (player) {\n      if (typeof player.getVolume === 'function') {\n        const v = player.getVolume();\n        if (typeof v === 'number' && !isNaN(v)) {\n          currentVol = v;\n        }\n      }\n      if (typeof player.isMuted === 'function') {\n        isMuted = player.isMuted();\n      }\n    } else if (queuedVolume !== null) {\n      currentVol = queuedVolume;\n    }\n\n    try {\n      window.dispatchEvent(\n        new CustomEvent(EVENT_VOLUME_STATUS, {\n          detail: {\n            volume: currentVol,\n            muted: isMuted,\n            hasPlayer: !!player\n          }\n        })\n      );\n    } catch (e) {}\n  }\n\n  // Listen for volume change requests from isolated content script\n  window.addEventListener(EVENT_SET_VOLUME, (event) => {\n    try {\n      let data = event.detail;\n      if (typeof data === 'string') {\n        try {\n          data = JSON.parse(data);\n        } catch (e) {\n          data = Number(data);\n        }\n      }\n\n      const vol = typeof data === 'object' && data !== null && typeof data.volume === 'number'\n        ? data.volume\n        : (typeof data === 'number' ? data : null);\n\n      if (vol !== null) {\n        applyVolume(vol, data?.reason || 'CustomEvent');\n      }\n    } catch (err) {\n      console.warn('[RetroFM MainWorld] Error processing volume event:', err);\n    }\n  });\n\n  // Also support window.postMessage for redundancy\n  window.addEventListener('message', (event) => {\n    if (event.source !== window || !event.data) return;\n    if (event.data.type === 'RETROFM_SET_VOLUME_MSG') {\n      const vol = typeof event.data.volume === 'number' ? event.data.volume : null;\n      if (vol !== null) {\n        applyVolume(vol, event.data.reason || 'postMessage');\n      }\n    } else if (event.data.type === 'RETROFM_QUERY_VOLUME_MSG') {\n      broadcastStatus();\n    }\n  });\n\n  // Reapply queued volume on video lifecycle events (song start / loadedmetadata / playing)\n  function attachMediaListeners(media) {\n    if (!media || media.__retroFmListenersAttached) return;\n    media.__retroFmListenersAttached = true;\n\n    const onMediaLifecycle = (evtType) => {\n      if (queuedVolume !== null) {\n        applyVolume(queuedVolume, `event:${evtType}`);\n      } else {\n        broadcastStatus();\n      }\n    };\n\n    // Earliest video hooks\n    media.addEventListener('loadstart', () => onMediaLifecycle('loadstart'));\n    media.addEventListener('loadedmetadata', () => onMediaLifecycle('loadedmetadata'));\n    media.addEventListener('canplay', () => onMediaLifecycle('canplay'));\n    media.addEventListener('playing', () => {\n      const player = getPlayer();\n      const currentVol = (player && typeof player.getVolume === 'function') ? player.getVolume() : 'unknown';\n      console.log(\n        `[RetroFM MainWorld] [${new Date().toISOString()}] Volume at moment playback started: player.getVolume()=${currentVol}, queuedVolume=${queuedVolume}`\n      );\n      onMediaLifecycle('playing');\n    });\n  }\n\n  functi